// Local opt-in code signing for the Picky app target.
//
// Defaults below reproduce the committed project behavior exactly: signing stays
// disabled, so plain Xcode/xcodebuild Debug builds are ad-hoc signed as before
// and contributors without an Apple Development certificate are unaffected.
//
// Why opting in matters: macOS TCC keeps one authorization record per
// (service, bundle id). An ad-hoc bundle's designated requirement is pinned to
// its cdhash, which changes on every build, so each rebuild invalidates the
// record shared with the signed app at build/dev-signed/export. Signing every
// Debug build with the same Apple Development certificate gives all local Picky
// copies one stable certificate-based requirement, and Microphone/Accessibility/
// Screen Recording grants survive rebuilds.
//
// To opt in, create Signing.local.xcconfig (git-ignored) next to this file:
//
//   PICKY_CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED = YES
//   PICKY_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOURTEAMID
//   CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development
//
// scripts/package-signed-app.sh keeps working either way because command-line
// build settings override xcconfig values.

PICKY_CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED = NO
PICKY_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
